# Testing Requirements

## Mandatory Tests
Every feature module MUST have tests for:

1. ✅ API Client (`[feature].api.test.ts`)
   - Test all API methods
   - Mock axios responses
   - Test error handling

2. ✅ Redux Slice (`[feature]Slice.test.ts`)
   - Test initial state
   - Test reducers
   - Test async thunks (pending, fulfilled, rejected)

3. ✅ Custom Hooks (`use[Feature].test.ts`)
   - Test hook behavior
   - Test Redux integration
   - Test side effects

4. ✅ Components (`[Component].test.tsx`)
   - Test rendering
   - Test user interactions
   - Test loading states
   - Test error states

## Test File Template

```typescript
import { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach } from 'vitest';
import { renderHook, waitFor } from '@testing-library/react';
import { Provider } from 'react-redux';
import { configureStore } from '@reduxjs/toolkit';
import featureReducer from '../reducers/featureSlice';

// Mock setup
vi.mock('../feature.api', () => ({
  featureApi: {
    getAll: vi.fn(),
    getById: vi.fn(),
  },
}));

describe('Feature Module', () => {
  let store: any;

  beforeEach(() => {
    store = configureStore({
      reducer: { feature: featureReducer },
    });
    vi.clearAllMocks();
  });

  describe('API Tests', () => {
    it('should fetch items successfully', async () => {
      // Test implementation
    });
  });

  describe('Slice Tests', () => {
    it('should handle initial state', () => {
      const state = featureReducer(undefined, { type: '' });
      expect(state.items).toEqual([]);
      expect(state.loading).toBe(false);
    });
  });

  describe('Hook Tests', () => {
    it('should fetch items on mount', async () => {
      // Test implementation
    });
  });
});
```

## Running Tests
```bash
npm run test              # Run all tests
npm run test:watch        # Watch mode
npm run test:coverage     # With coverage
```

## Coverage Requirements
- Aim for 80%+ code coverage
- All critical paths must be tested
- See [auth module tests](mdc:src/modules/auth/__tests__) for examples
